{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a5ab73ff14753bd9", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# ProDiff: Progressive Fast Diffusion Model For High-Quality Text-to-Speech\narXiv: 2207.06389\nAuthors: Rongjie Huang, Zhou Zhao, Huadai Liu, Jinglin Liu, Chenye Cui, Yi Ren\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We analyze and compare different diffusion parameterizations in text-to-speech synthesis, showing that directly predicting clean data accelerates sampling better than estimating the gradient.\n  2. We propose ProDiff, which parameterizes the denoising model to directly predict clean data and uses knowledge distillation to reduce data variance for sharper predictions.\n  3. We demonstrate that ProDiff requires only 2 iterations to synthesize high-fidelity mel-spectrograms while maintaining competitive quality and diversity, enabling practical real-time deployment.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3ce61c3e-6276-4a5e-9583-ae8c8bc39343", "uuid": "e293a7e8-1e8a-44cb-abe4-423c8721ea82", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:13:35.233Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# ProDiff: Progressive Fast Diffusion Model For High-Quality Text-to-Speech\narXiv: 2207.06389\nAuthors: Rongjie Huang, Zhou Zhao, Huadai Liu, Jinglin Liu, Chenye Cui, Yi Ren\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We analyze and compare different diffusion parameterizations in text-to-speech synthesis, showing that directly predicting clean data accelerates sampling better than estimating the gradient.\n  2. We propose ProDiff, which parameterizes the denoising model to directly predict clean data and uses knowledge distillation to reduce data variance for sharper predictions.\n  3. We demonstrate that ProDiff requires only 2 iterations to synthesize high-fidelity mel-spectrograms while maintaining competitive quality and diversity, enabling practical real-time deployment.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b4fa0e09bc8ad217", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# FastSpeech 2: Fast and High-Quality End-to-End Text to Speech\narXiv: 2006.04558\nAuthors: Yi Ren, Chenxu Hu, Xu Tan, Tao Qin, Sheng Zhao, Zhou Zhao, Tie-Yan Liu\nYear: 2020 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. FastSpeech 2 achieves a 3x training speed-up over FastSpeech by simplifying the training pipeline.\n  2. FastSpeech 2 alleviates the one-to-many mapping problem in TTS and achieves better voice quality.\n  3. FastSpeech 2s further simplifies the inference pipeline for speech synthesis while maintaining high voice quality, by directly generating speech waveform from text.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-快速生成", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3ce61c3e-6276-4a5e-9583-ae8c8bc39343", "uuid": "03f7143a-1a40-447d-9f4d-50e0c2959bca", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:13:35.527Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# FastSpeech 2: Fast and High-Quality End-to-End Text to Speech\narXiv: 2006.04558\nAuthors: Yi Ren, Chenxu Hu, Xu Tan, Tao Qin, Sheng Zhao, Zhou Zhao, Tie-Yan Liu\nYear: 2020 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. FastSpeech 2 achieves a 3x training speed-up over FastSpeech by simplifying the training pipeline.\n  2. FastSpeech 2 alleviates the one-to-many mapping problem in TTS and achieves better voice quality.\n  3. FastSpeech 2s further simplifies the inference pipeline for speech synthesis while maintaining high voice quality, by directly generating speech waveform from text.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-快速生成", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9b1a33c323690fb4", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Minimizing Modality Gap from the Input Side: Your Speech LLM Can Be a Prosody-Aware Text LLM\narXiv: 2605.05927\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes TextPro-SLM, a speech LLM that minimizes the text-speech modality gap from the input side by making spoken input resemble that of a prosody-aware text LLM.\n  2. Introduces WhisperPro, a unified speech encoder that produces synchronized text tokens and prosody embeddings to capture both linguistic content and paralinguistic information.\n  3. Trains the LLM backbone with coupled objectives to preserve the original text LLM's semantic capabilities via knowledge distillation while learning paralinguistic understanding.\n  4. Achieves the lowest modality gap among leading SLMs at both 3B and 7B scales while delivering strong performance on paralinguistic understanding tasks.\n  5. Demonstrates data efficiency by requiring only roughly 1,000 hours of audio for LLM training to effectively reduce the modality gap.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3ce61c3e-6276-4a5e-9583-ae8c8bc39343", "uuid": "7a049a6a-9a73-47b4-b4e4-fe3cfefcc384", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:13:35.818Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Minimizing Modality Gap from the Input Side: Your Speech LLM Can Be a Prosody-Aware Text LLM\narXiv: 2605.05927\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes TextPro-SLM, a speech LLM that minimizes the text-speech modality gap from the input side by making spoken input resemble that of a prosody-aware text LLM.\n  2. Introduces WhisperPro, a unified speech encoder that produces synchronized text tokens and prosody embeddings to capture both linguistic content and paralinguistic information.\n  3. Trains the LLM backbone with coupled objectives to preserve the original text LLM's semantic capabilities via knowledge distillation while learning paralinguistic understanding.\n  4. Achieves the lowest modality gap among leading SLMs at both 3B and 7B scales while delivering strong performance on paralinguistic understanding tasks.\n  5. Demonstrates data efficiency by requiring only roughly 1,000 hours of audio for LLM training to effectively reduce the modality gap.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9be0c95d7a8f63c7", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# MambaVoiceCloning: Efficient and Expressive Text-to-Speech via State-Space Modeling and Diffusion Control\narXiv: 2604.00292\nAuthors: Sahil Kumar, Namrataben Patel, Honggang Wang, Youshan Zhang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A diffusion-based TTS system with a fully SSM-only inference-time conditioning path spanning text, rhythm, and prosody under a fixed decoder.\n  2. A gated bidirectional Mamba fusion with AdaLN that improves long-range prosody stability and reduces drift on multi-sentence and out-of-distribution text.\n  3. Protocol- and capacity-matched baselines that isolate the architectural impact of removing inference-time attention.\n  4. A deployment-oriented analysis covering memory usage, throughput, SSM hyperparameter sensitivity, long-form behavior, and finite look-ahead streaming, demonstrating predictable linear-time characteristics.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3ce61c3e-6276-4a5e-9583-ae8c8bc39343", "uuid": "944571ca-35d6-4eb9-9947-8dadc1e19dd4", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:13:36.113Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# MambaVoiceCloning: Efficient and Expressive Text-to-Speech via State-Space Modeling and Diffusion Control\narXiv: 2604.00292\nAuthors: Sahil Kumar, Namrataben Patel, Honggang Wang, Youshan Zhang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A diffusion-based TTS system with a fully SSM-only inference-time conditioning path spanning text, rhythm, and prosody under a fixed decoder.\n  2. A gated bidirectional Mamba fusion with AdaLN that improves long-range prosody stability and reduces drift on multi-sentence and out-of-distribution text.\n  3. Protocol- and capacity-matched baselines that isolate the architectural impact of removing inference-time attention.\n  4. A deployment-oriented analysis covering memory usage, throughput, SSM hyperparameter sensitivity, long-form behavior, and finite look-ahead streaming, demonstrating predictable linear-time characteristics.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
